  "design": {
    "decision": "Every trick becomes a puzzle about winning cheaply: ruff with the [2♠] instead of the [K♠], hold low cards of long suits for the end, and prefer Opening effects that keep cards low over ones that raise them.",
    "opponent": "Obvious after the first low win; opponents overruff low trumps, keep honors to beat late low cards, and avoid giving the team ruffing chances.",
    "rationale": "The Low Cards build-around: a repeated ×1.5 that compounds on two or three cheap wins (the legendary budget is ×2-×3 broadly). It changes how a whole run is drafted, toward low [♠]s, low-card rule benders, and away from raise effects, which is what a legendary should do.",
